.TH FASTRDP-DEFAULTS 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-defaults \- default configuration files of the fastrdp packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-defaults status
.RI [ package ...]
.br
.B fastrdp-defaults diff
.RI [ file ...]
.br
.B fastrdp-defaults install
.I package
.br
.B fastrdp-defaults purge
.I package
.SH DESCRIPTION
The fastrdp packages ship a working default for each configuration file in
.I /etc
that fastrdp needs (for example
.IR /etc/fastrdp/broker.toml ,
.IR /etc/fastrdp/proxy.ini ,
.IR /etc/xrdp/xrdp.ini ).
They are not dpkg conffiles: the Ansible roles of fast-rdp-server write the same files,
and dpkg would ask about them on every upgrade.
.PP
The package scripts run
.B install
for each package. A file gets fastrdp's version when it is missing, when it is still
the version installed last time (unchanged since), or when it is upstream's default
(xrdp). A file you changed is never touched; the command then says once per new
fastrdp version where fastrdp's version is.
.B purge
(on
.BR "apt purge" )
removes the files that are still unchanged.
.PP
.B status
prints every file with its state:
.I fastrdp default
(as shipped),
.I changed locally
or
.IR missing .
.B diff
shows your changes against fastrdp's version (diff \-u).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/<package>/defaults.list
The files of a package: DEST MODE OWNER GROUP SOURCE [if=PATH] [also=FILE].
.TP
.I /var/lib/fastrdp/defaults/<package>
Checksums of the installed and the shipped version of each file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-check-host (8),
docs/manual-setup.md
